    "column_index": 3,
    "column_header": "Particulars.",
    "raw_text": "This famine is generally known by the name of \"Soodtala\" (i. e. appertaining to 1847), derived from the Sumvut year in which it took place. Grain was sold at the rate of 15 seers (Suratee) per Rupee. The people were in great distress owing to the scarcity of grain. Their sufferings, however, were alleviated by the large supply of cocoanuts and dates shipped from other ports, and sold at a cheap rate. This information is traditional, and is obtained from Dajee Rughoonath Dasaee.",
    "value_numeric": null,
    "unit": "Rs",
    "is_null_or_leader": false,
    "arithmetic_verified": false
  },
